[tutorial]
//[] receives a number,if the number whose prior to another number which "Another one [] receives a number", the correnpondence performing sequence prior to "Another one"
//we call it "DIALOG"
//NOTE为了保证原子性 无论是host 还是 client 都需要做完操作后 最后 才会设置Flag
//NOTE 基本的顺序的就是 host设置1 host等待 client有消息发送就设置0 host接受 host处理 host设置回1  继续下一个循环 host和client本质上都是同一个等待模型

[0]
data: <PlatformIndependentAddressType>
length: <an 32bit value for data length>
requires length range [32MB,4GB],(length & (64-1)) == 0,length is the power of 2,addr of data,(AddrOfData & (64-1) == 0)

[1] initialize

data Addr Space
<double word,4byte for Hello> <4byte address length>
LowAddr <-> HighAddr
---All Zero Filled---

<address length> means the whole length of addr space, not include 0!
which in Hello:
1st word 1st 1byte HelloMessage
1st word 2nd 1byte padding for alignment
2st word 1st 1byte Low8bitAddr pcapability mask
  which in capability mask
  bit0: does it suports UMONITOR extension   1 yes 0 no
  bit1: does it supports PhysAddr passthrough 1 yes 0 no
  bit2: client error return bit,host is expected to set the bit as 0
  bit3-7: reserved
2st word 2st 1byte padding for alignment

//note 4byte address length is a 4byte unsigned int
host init
host send the a proper message to client
host set 1 to LowAddr of Hello in the end
then host wait the 2byte short for Hello, no timeout (aka. host wait)

client will init now
client will check this Hello msg first, then check the accuracy of capability mask, and compare the Client-side data size and Host-side data size(length) to ensure that the length are accurate
client if it's inaccurate set 1 to capability mask bit2 and write 0 to LowAddr of Hello,set 0 to LowAddr of Hello simultaneously to notify the host,then interrupt&end this DIALOG
client if it's accurate just set 0 to LowAddr of Hello to notify the host in the end
client wait for the LowAddr of Hello(aka. client wait)

when host received the result,check the ErrorMask then
no matter what,the host will clean the whole Addr Space! filled with zero

[2] functions dispatch

data Addr Space
<2byte ushort for Flag> <2byte int for split number> <4byte bytes per split>
LowAddr <-> HighAddr
---All Zero Filled---

requires <split number> * <bytes per split> == <length>
revision: requires: (<bytes per split> % 4) == 0
revision: requires: (<bytes per split> % 64) == 0,<bytes per split> be the power of 2,bytes per split >= 8,split number >= 1
note: the max vlaue of split number is 65535 unsigned int, requires <split number> ge(>=) 1
note: the bytes per split is 4byte unsigned int, requires the <bytes per split> must be the power of 2 and greater|equals than 2MB
which in 2byte short for Flag:
  LowAddr FlagItSelf
  HighAddr ErrorCode
  which in ErrorCode
    0x0 OK
    0x1 ILLEGAL FUNC COUNT
    0x2 ILLEGAL SPACE COUNT
    ge 0x3 OTHER ERROR,reserved
    
host prepare the functions set the <split number>,<bytes per split>
host set the 1 to LowAddr of Flag
then host wait the LowAddr of Flag, no timeout

client received the message, prepare the functions offsets
if clients can't set the function-space will set the Error Code to HighAddr of Flag,then set 0 to LowAddr of Flag to notify the host,interrupt&close this DIALOG
else direclty set 0 to LowAddr of Flag to notify the host
client wait,no timeout

host received the Flag,check the ErrorCode
finally,host will set all zero filled
thus,all of client & host located each the function's head Flag

[3] functions content

(<function head> <function body>) ...
LowAddr <-> HighAddr
---All Zero Filled--- 

requires <2word(4byte) function body> + <function head> == <bytes per split>
which in <function head>
  which in function body
  1st word,1st byte hello msg
  1st word,2nd byte padding for alignment
  2nd word,1st byte FuncNumber
  2nd word,2nd byte padding for alignment
  which in FuncNumber
    0x0 huge page SHM,see blow
    0x1 SHM
    0x2 rpc function
    ... reserved no function
revision the address of function body,must be alignas 64byte,i.e. (addrtolong % 64 == 0)
the huge page SHM
  this is used by non-SHM function,it can be read only while non-SHM function's Flag is 1(shm)
  the huge page SHM occupies one or more splits,and there's mere one Flag is available
the huge page SHM layout
<huge SHM Flag> <4byte bytes for huge SHM size> <huge SHM body>
LowAddr <-> HighAddr
---All Zero Filled--- 
which in the <huge SHM Flag>
  as same as function head
  1st word,1st byte,reserved
  1st word,2nd byte padding for alignment
  2nd word,1st byte,constant 0x0
  2nd word,2nd byte padding for alignment
requires <huge SHM Flag> + <huge SHM size> +<huge SHM body> = <any_unsign_integer> * <bytes per split>
requires value of <SHM size> == <huge SHM Flag> + <if exists huge SHM size> + <huge SHM body>
revision: requires (<Huge SHM size> % 64) == 0,<Huge SHM size> is the power of 2, alternative representation Huge SHM Size % bytes per split == 0
NOTE: make the SHM space inhabits on the tail space of <data> as mush as possible,but it's not a contraint

the SHM
similar to huge page SHM,the SHM is similar to huge page SHM,but they still have some differents
the SHM layout
<SHM Flag> <SHM body>
LowAddr <-> HighAddr
---All Zero Filled---
differ to huge page SHM,the SHM(<SHM Flag> + <SHM body>) occupies <bytes per split> bytes
which in <SHM Flag>
  LowAddr Reserved DONOT READWRITE 0x1 for constant
  HighAddr Reserved DONOT READ 0x1 for constant
the SHM is used by Non-SHM functions as well




the rpc function

a super simple rpc function

NOTE: rpc do not check or match any size|type|offset information, the parameter,return info must be convented between client&host

layout
<rpc flag> <rpc body>
LowAddr <-> HighAddr
---All Zero Filled---

<which in rpc flag>
1st byte 1st byte call Flag
1st byte 2nd byte padded for alignment
2nd 1st byte reserved for constant 0x2
2nd 2nd byte padded for alignment

<which in rpc body>
  <parameters> <result>
  LowAddr <-> HighAddr
  there's not fixed size for all

in implementations,parameters and result can passed via SHM,huge page SHM but there's no standard method,rely entirely on the conventions
e.g. parameter is a 64byte struct,but return is a super large buffer which beyonds the <bytes per split>, the host&client can define a protocol where host creates a huge page,map/copy the memory to such huge SHM,the result in <rpc body> can be wrote just 4byte that it stand for the offset of <splits>,actually it looks like another representation of pointer

host&client's convention must guarantee the "<parameters> + <result> <= <bytes per split>"

concrete rpc procedure similar to the before steps:
1. host set the Function to 1 to Flag, except that, there's no other read&write, host wait the Flag to be 0
2. the client pass the args,the host is waiting simultaneously
3. client pull the Flag to 0 to notify the host,client wait the Flag to be 1
4. host read the arg,clean args,write the result after args,pull back to 1
5. client received the Flag,read the result,end
6. client clean result
7. back to 1

rpcs are anonymous,the concrete steps also depends on the conventions

one last requirements <add all functions include flags&sizes> == <length>

revision: every write&read operation in this area,must align as 4 byte